      "reasoning": "Both videos follow essentially the same trajectory. They realize a visible right turn, a hold and a left return, and they reproduce the start layout briefly around frames 120-124 with consistent landmark identity. Both then over-rotate left and settle on a view offset from frame 0, so neither cleanly recovers the starting viewpoint. This is a camera-control or yaw-magnitude issue, not memory loss. A is marginally preferred because its overshoot region adds less invented content. B introduces a prominent new red-shirted person and table in the foreground, which moves its final frame further from the original scene. The difference is small, so confidence is low."
